course: dictionary
lesson: 13220
title: A gabled roof
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A gabled house has a pointed, triangle-shaped part of wall at the top, under the two sloping sides of the roof. That triangle is called a gable. «The old farmhouse had a gabled roof and two tall chimneys.» The word gabled tells you the roof has these triangle walls.
explain: You can spot a gable by looking at the shape. It has a point at the top and a flat bottom edge, and it sits under the two slopes of a roof. «Mia drew a gabled house with a triangle on top of a square.» Her triangle is the gable, and the square is the rest of the house.
explain: Gabled is an adjective. It describes a noun, like a house, a roof or an inn. «The gabled inn looked cosy in the snow.» Read the words around it: a roof and a house are the things that can be gabled, so you can guess the meaning from the context.
fact: A gable is the pointed, triangle-shaped part of a wall under the two sloping sides of a roof.
fact: «Gabled» means having a gable or gables.
fact: In maths, a house drawn as a square with a triangle on top has a gable.
fact: Old houses and inns in stories are often gabled, and they can look cosy or mysterious.
fact: Context clues help: the words «roof» and «house» near «gabled» tell you what it describes.
exercise: «The old farmhouse had a gabled roof.» What does gabled mean? | Made of wood only | Painted bright red | Having a flat roof with no slopes | *Having a gable, the pointed triangle-shaped wall under the two slopes of a roof
exercise: What is a gable? | *The pointed, triangle-shaped part of a wall under the two sloping sides of a roof | The round window at the top of a church | The path to the front door | The chimney on a house
exercise: «Mia drew a gabled house with a triangle on top of a square.» Find and copy one word that describes the house. | drew | *gabled | triangle | square
test: Which house has a gabled roof? | A long, low wall | A flat box with no roof | *A house with a pointed triangle-shaped wall under the two sloping sides of its roof | A tree with round leaves
test: Ben draws a house as a square with a triangle on top. What is the triangle called? | Chimney | Window | Door | *Gable
exam: «The gabled house on the hill looked mysterious in the fog.» What does gabled mean? | *Having a gable, the pointed triangle-shaped wall under the two sloping sides of a roof | Very tall and thin | Having no roof at all | Having a round window
